Package: workspaceos
Version: 3.0.0
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: libc6, libstdc++6, zlib1g, libgcc-s1 | libgcc1, wmctrl, xdotool, x11-utils, x11-xserver-utils
Recommends: gsettings-desktop-schemas, xbindkeys, xz-utils
Suggests: xdg-utils
Installed-Size: 95000
Maintainer: WorkspaceOS <noreply@workspaceos.local>
Description: Hyprland-inspired workspaces, tiling and hotkeys — natively on Linux
 WorkspaceOS is a native Linux daemon (no Wine) that adds Hyprland-style
 workspaces and a Dwindle BSP tiling engine to your existing desktop.
 .
 On install it automatically registers your WorkspaceOS keymap with the
 running desktop environment — Cinnamon custom keybindings on Linux Mint,
 MATE run-commands, or an xbindkeys fallback — so Win+1..9 switch
 workspaces, Win+Shift+1..9 send windows, and the full tiling keymap
 (Win+H/J/K/L focus, Win+Shift+H/J/K/L move, Win+Ctrl+H/J/K/L resize,
 float, togglesplit, preselect) works right away. Changing hotkeys in
 config.json re-applies the keymap automatically.
 .
 Also included: rule-based auto-assignment of windows to workspaces,
 window commands (close/maximize/center/fullscreen via Win+W/M/C/F) and
 a CLI (`workspaceos status`, `workspaceos keys`, `workspaceos retile`).
 .
 The daemon reuses the same Dwindle layout core and the same config.json
 format as the Windows build.
